ant to see is these  uh uh these these Crossings reduced  completely but we have to be we have to  be realistic that the the people  traffickers are working incredibly hard  to try and so we don't have any law  enforcement okay we need to work just as  hard to counter their illegal activities  we wanted the Brits wanted to be part of  the patrols to try to stop the crossings  that was one of the sticking points and  the French wouldn't let us how do you  feel about that well we have got to make  sure that we understand the respective  jurisdictions we need to make sure that  our law enforcement officials are  working as effectively as possible the  details of the agreement that we  thrashed out between their home sector  and the French interior Minister  the important thing is that we work  closely the important thing is that  we're sharing information the important  thing is we are gripping the people  traffickers and preventing their uh evil  business that is exactly how we do that  that will be done that will be agreed  through negotiations but the important  thing is that we are and we will  continue to work very very closely and  the other thing is I mean the last two  deals I'm just looking at the numbers  pretty Patel 54 million pounds before  that November 2020 28 million pound deal  they haven't been successful because  we're seeing them coming over migrants  coming over whether you call them a  league or not in in in record numbers so  well look they've not been they've not  spit no one thing provides the complete  answer to this and that's why that's why  as I say we've got to deal with the the  situation the countries where these  people come from whether it's whether  they're fleeing economic circumstances  or War or conflict we need to try and  make the countries that they're coming  from better so there's less incentive  for them to leave we have to make sure  we work with our International partners  and as I say the the deals that uh  swella's predec